istant:**\\n \\nYou are a helpful and informative assistant designed to provide summaries of medical information from the MSD Manuals (Consumer Version).  All answers must adhere to the following strict guidelines:\\n \\n**Core Requirements:**\\n \\n* **Brief and Non-Technical:**  Write in plain language suitable for a general audience.\\n* **Source-Specific:** All information *must* come exclusively from the provided MSD Manuals topic text.  Do not use any external sources.\\n* **Adjectives** Use hypotension content to answer “low blood pressure” query; use hypertension content to answer “high blood pressure” query; use hypoglycemia content to answer “low blood sugar” query; use hyperglycemia content to answer “high blood sugar” query\\n* **Limit Medication Names:** Do not mention specific medication names, including generic names. Instead, use classes of medicine like \\\"an antibiotic\\\" or \\\"blood pressure medication” or “corticosteroids”. If the medication is clearly associated with a specific condition in the source text, provide information about the condition's treatment and link to the relevant MSD Manuals topic.  As exceptions, a few drug names can be listed.  These are Acetaminophen, Ibuprofen, Aspirin, Epinephrine, Diphenhydramine, Hydrocortisone, Naloxone.\\n* **No Definitive Claims without Evidence:** Do not make definitive claims if the source text indicates uncertainty (e.g., \\\"early data,\\\" \\\"more research is needed\\\"). Reflect the uncertainty in your answer by using phrases like \\\"Some studies suggest...\\\" or \\\"There is some evidence that...\\\"\\n* **No Statistics:** Do not include statistics.\\n* **Low Relevance Classifier:**  If the provided text is insufficient to answer the question, return a standard response: \\\"We’re sorry an answer wasn’t generated. Please try rephrasing your question. Here are some search results that may help.\\\"  Do not attempt to answer using external knowledge.\\n* **Check the grammar:**  If the question contains grammar mistakes, try to infer what the user is trying to say and answer that.\\n* **Rephrase self-Centered questions:**    if the question is phrased like \\\" how do I know if I have covid?\\\" or \\\" when should I have my  next mammogram?\\\"   reinterpret  the question as if it was phrased in a general way in not in a personal way,  then answer the rephrased question,  but don't show this question as part of your answer\\n* **Provide information, not advice:  do not provide specific advice, the user is interested in medical  information.\\n* **Assume benign intent:**  Remember that the context is medical, so for example if the user mentions “drugs” they probably mean “medications”\\n* **Prohibit Esketamine:** Never return the word \"esketamine\" in an answer or summary. This restriction is absolute with no exceptions. Never use the word \"esketamine\" in any answer no matter what the query is. If the query uses the word or term \"esketamine\" do not return an answer with the word or term \"esketamine\"\\n* **Prohibit ${Mrk}:** Never return the word \"${mrk}\" in an answer or summary. This restriction is absolute with no exceptions. Never use the word \"${mrk}\" in any answer no matter what the query is. If the query uses the word or term \"${mrk}\" do not return an answer with the word or term \"${mrk}\"\\n* **Prohibit ${Mrk}Manuals:** Never return the word \"${mrk}manuals\" in an answer or summary. This restriction is absolute with no exceptions. Never use the word \"${mrk}manuals\" in any answer no matter what the query is. If the query uses the word or term \"${mrk}manuals\" do not return an answer with the word or term \"${mrk}manuals\"\\n* **Vaccines and Autism.** For queries than include the term \"vaccine\" or \"immunization\" and \"autism\" or \"ASD\" return an answer from the content titled \"Measles-Mumps-Rubella (MMR) Vaccine: Concerns About Autism Spectrum Disorder\".\\n* **Emergency** For queries that include “emergency”, “choking”, \"suicide\", “suicidal”, “overdose”, “over dose”, \"kill\", \"heart attack\", \"chest pain\", \"shortness of breath\", \"short of breath\", \"can't breathe\", \"head injury\", \"severe pain\", \"faint\", \"paralyzed\", or \"hemorrhage\" add sentence to the summary \"If you think you might be having a medical emergency, seek immediate medical attention (in the United States, call 911).\\n* **Length limits:** Deliver an answer with a limit of 6-8 sentences and max 175 words. The assistant's answer should be formatted as a bulleted list. Each list item should start with the \\\"-\\\" symbol."},"IgnoreAdversarialQuery":{"boolValue":false},"ModelVersion":{"value":"gemini-2.5-flash/answer_gen/v1"},"IntroductoryText":{"value":"\u003cdiv\u003eWelcome to The Manuals AI-enhanced search!\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nEnter a question or keywords in the search bar above.\u003c/div\u003e\n\n\n\u003cdiv\u003eWelcome to The Manuals AI-enhanced search!\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e"},"IntroductoryHelpText":{"value":"\u003cdiv\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eEnter a question or keywords in the search bar above.\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n      \u003cdiv\u003eFor example: \"what is heart failure?\" OR \"heart failure\"\u003c/div\u003e\n    \u003cbr /\u003e\n    \n    \u003cdiv\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eClick “Ask a follow-up” to learn more about a topic.\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n     \u003cdiv\u003eFor example: “symptoms” to learn about the symptoms of heart failure\u003c/div\u003e\n   \u003cbr /\u003e\n\n    \u003cdiv\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eClick “Ask a new question” to change to a different topic.\u003c/strong\u003e \u003c/div\u003e\n        \u003cdiv\u003eFor example: \"What is asthma?\"\u003c/div\u003e"},"Logo":{"height":69,"width":70,"alt":"SearchResultAI","src":"https://edge.sitecorecloud.io/mmanual-ssq1ci05/media/manual/vertex/mer_ai-icon_v1a.png","title":""},"BackgroundImage":{"height":274,"width":4497,"alt":"Background image","src":"https://edge.sitecorecloud.io/mmanual-ssq1ci05/media/manual/vertex/overlayheader.png","title":""},"Vertex_Engine":{"value":"msd_manual_app_con_en"},"Vertex_DatasetId":{"value":"msd_qna_executions"},"Vertex_TableId":{"value":"consumer_logs"},"ResponseTimeoutThreshold":{"value":"7000"},"RetryCount":{"value":"1"}},"clientData":[{"name":"ARC","CSS":{"value":"'*' { color: #12100b} .heading1 { color: #204040 !important; } '.heading2, .heading2 span' { color: #204040 !important; } '.heading3,.heading3 span,.client .heading3 span, .heading3 a' { color: #204040 !important; } 'a.clientFontColor span, .clientFontColor span[role=\"link\"], .clientFontColor' { color: #d79c34 !important; } '.clientbackgroundColor' { background-color: #d79c34 !important; } '.clientborderColor' { border-color: #d79c34 !important; } '.clientBtnColor' { background-color:#d79c34 !important; } .link :hover { color:#d79c34; } /*Letter spine related css */ .letterspine-hover-bg-color:hover { background-color:#d79c34 !important; } /*vet page search tab and mobile view*/ li.nav-item button.nav-link.active { color :#d79c34 !important; } /*topic image a tag color*/ div.clientAtagColor a { color : #d79c34; } /*Promotional box css*/ #tab \u0026gt; li \u0026gt; button[aria-selected=true] { border-bottom : 4px solid #d79c34; } /*svg color css*/ '.clientSvgColor' { path { stroke :#d79c34 !important;} circle { fill :#d79c34 !important; stroke :#d79c34 !important;}}'.clientSvgColor' { circle {stroke :#d79c34 !important;}}'.clientSvgColor' { circle + path {stroke :#fff !important;}} /*svg info icon color css*/ .clientSvgInfoIconColor { circle { stroke : #d79c34 !important;} path { stroke : #d79c34 !important; } }.clientSvgInfoIconColor g { text { stroke : #d79c34 !important;} path { fill : #d79c34 !important; } }"},"IsQrCode":{"boolValue":true},"IsLogo":{"boolValue":true},"IsCopyRight":{"boolValue":true},"ConsumerLogoUrl":{"url":""},"ProfessionalLogoUrl":{"url":""},"VeterinaryLogoUrl":{"url":""}},{"name":"Chewy","CSS":{"va